{"id": "EUVD-2026-103338", "enisaUuid": "1b158bb7-5ff0-39ba-a1a1-5d594969f12b", "description": "FreeRDP versions from 2.0.0 before 3.32.0 contain a heap out-of-bounds write in the server hash-callback NTLM path that fails to validate the MIC offset. Unauthenticated attackers can send a crafted AUTHENTICATE_MESSAGE with a backward session-key offset and MIC offset to write 16 zero bytes beyond the allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:40:26", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-cmgx-558f-vh67", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-2.0.0-before-3.32.0-heap-out-of-bounds-write-via-ntlm-mic-offset"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111880", "GHSA-98x3-97xw-cfqr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f3781371-f473-39b9-97cd-0a459a2fcc2c", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f725948d-3e60-3703-a6b6-06af24e48a45", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}